{"name":"Fairway","hex":"#477050","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fairway","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The area between the tee and the green, where the grass is cut short.","Any tract of land free from obstacles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairway"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golf course","blocks":[{"text":"A golf course is the grounds on which the sport of golf is played. It consists of a series of holes, each consisting of a tee box, a fairway, the rough and other hazards, and a green with a cylindrical hole in the ground, known as a \"cup\". The cup holds a flagstick, known as a \"pin\". A standard round of golf consists of 18 holes, and as such most courses contain 18 distinct holes; however, there are many 9-hole courses and some that have holes with shared fairways or greens. There are also courses with a non-standard number of holes, such as 12 or 14."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Golf_course_Golfplatz_Wittenbeck_Mecklenburg_Ostsee_Baltic_Sea_Germany.jpg/330px-Golf_course_Golfplatz_Wittenbeck_Mecklenburg_Ostsee_Baltic_Sea_Germany.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golf_course","wikidata":"Q1048525"},{"title":"Fairway (navigation)","blocks":[{"text":"Fairway is a part of a water body containing the navigable channel, a route suitable for ships of the larger size."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairway_(navigation)","wikidata":"Q1138251"},{"title":"Fairway (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Fairway (1925–1948) was a British Thoroughbred racehorse and sire. Fairway was the best horse of his generation in Britain at two, three and four years old, winning the St Leger Stakes, the Champion Stakes (twice) and the Eclipse Stakes. He retired as a five-year-old in 1930 and went on to become a successful and influential sire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Fairway_%28horse%29.jpg/330px-Fairway_%28horse%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairway_(horse)","wikidata":"Q5430908"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Golf_and_Country_Club_de_Bossey_and_the_A40_motorway_near_Geneve_in_France.jpg/500px-Golf_and_Country_Club_de_Bossey_and_the_A40_motorway_near_Geneve_in_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Golf_and_Country_Club_de_Bossey_and_the_A40_motorway_near_Geneve_in_France.jpg/1280px-Golf_and_Country_Club_de_Bossey_and_the_A40_motorway_near_Geneve_in_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Golf_and_Country_Club_de_Bossey_and_the_A40_motorway_near_Geneve_in_France.jpg/500px-Golf_and_Country_Club_de_Bossey_and_the_A40_motorway_near_Geneve_in_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial view of a golf course in France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGolf_and_Country_Club_de_Bossey_and_the_A40_motorway_near_Geneve_in_France.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Kytajakoulu.JPG/500px-Kytajakoulu.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Kytajakoulu.JPG/1280px-Kytajakoulu.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Kytajakoulu.JPG/500px-Kytajakoulu.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kytäjä Golf in Kytäjä, Hyvinkää, Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKytajakoulu.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/First_Hole%2